  pages:
  - "As Vratimor\u2019s body crumbled to dust, the Acorn called out to the Saint.
    Understanding its summons, he placed it upon the castle floor. The moment the
    seed touched the cold stone, it took root. In an instant, an oak greater than
    any ever known burst forth, its roots tearing through the Lich\u2019s castle
    and reducing it to ruin, while its branches blazed with golden radiance, driving
    back the Darkness and rekindling hope throughout the world."
  - '"And so ends the legend of the Saint."


    "That is not quite how I remember
    it. It began much the same, true, but it went more like this..."'
  - 'With love

    PHANTOM DEVS'
